# Run eslint --fix over the files being committed.
#
# `import/order` is an error-level rule, and before this hook existed the only
# thing running it was CI — so it was discovered after a push, three times in one
# fortnight (see c4d6071). Worse, the rule only covered `src/`, so the unlinted
# Electron main process had no canonical import order at all and two branches
# appending to the same block conflicted on every rebase.
#
# Fixing it here means neither happens: the order is settled before the commit
# exists, so CI has nothing to catch and merges converge instead of colliding.
pnpm exec lint-staged
